+# 32-bit x86 has no PC-relative data addressing. Going through the GOT costs a
+# call/pop pair and two more instructions on every dispatch, which measured
+# 25% of a tight loop on an Atom Z520. The address is an absolute immediate
+# instead; the linker turns it into a text relocation, which Haiku's
+# runtime_loader applies, at the cost of the LLInt's text pages becoming
+# private to the process.
+def x86LoadLabelAddress32(asmLabel, dstOperand)
+    $asm.puts "movl $#{asmLabel}, #{dstOperand}"
+end
